From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=96zcan=20O=C4=9Fuz?= <ozcan@oyd.org.tr>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:01:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Berrak: nothing leaves the device; no proprietary
 libraries

Ported from Berrak 0.x onto Focus 159, adjusted for what upstream changed:

- Crash reporting: no Socorro or Sentry service, so no "send" prompt and the
  crash screen's consent checkbox is hidden. lib-crash-sentry and the
  Sentry SDK are not built in.
- Telemetry: upstream now hard-codes general telemetry off. The new daily
  usage ping (opt-in for Klar) still reports to Mozilla, so it is never
  started and its settings switch is removed.
- Nimbus gets no server. Upstream now fetches experiments from Mozilla's
  remote settings under the Klar app name; only bundled experiments apply.
- No Google Play Services: com.google.android.gms is excluded; GeckoView's
  WebAuthn backend needs it, so security.webauth.webauthn is set false
  through the GeckoRuntime config file. No Play Core: the in-app review
  prompt becomes a no-op. AD_ID is stripped from the merged manifest.
- Help, privacy notice, terms and manifesto links go to Berrak's docs (the
  terms link to its MPL-2.0 licence); SupportUtilsTest pins them.

Verified: klarDebug builds; its dex has no com.google.android.gms, io.sentry
or com.google.android.play classes; SupportUtilsTest passes.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ec3g34YeceWefbDxePbgre
